@ 15.2.7 - Proto-Eskimo to Siberian Yup’ik
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Swadesh, Morris (1952), “Unaaliq and Proto Eskimo IV: Diachronic
# 			Notes”, International Journal of American Linguistics, Vol. 18, No. 3 (Jul., 1952), pp.
# 			166–171
	C:[+ long] > C
	S > ∅ / #_F
	s > t͡s
	t͡s > t͡ʃ
	C:[+voice] > C:[-voice] / next to {S,s,l̥}
	ɣ ʁ > k q / _#
	ə > a /
	ə > ∅ / #_
	i > ∅ / #C:[+dental]_C:[+dental]V
	a > ∅ / C:[+velar]_C:[+velar]
	F:[+voice] > F:[-voice] / adjacent to {S,t͡s}
	F:[+voice] > S / l̥_
	
	t > s / _{k,q}
	u > a / a_
	ə > i / {u,a}_
	v > ∅ / u:[+short]_V:[+short]
	v > ∅ / V:[+short]_u:[+short]
	u > ∅ / #_vV
	iv > j / #_u
	s > d͡ʒ / {i,u}_V
	d͡ʒ > ∅ / i_i
	ə > ∅ / _d͡ʒ{a,u} // #U
	a > ∅ / _d͡ʒa // #U
	in > d͡ʒ / _u (possibly only word-initially?)